    "Description": "The kernel packages contain the Linux kernel, the core of any Linux operating system.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* kernel: selinux: fix overlayfs mmap() and mprotect() access checks (CVE-2026-46054)\n\n* kernel: Arm Processors: Privilege escalation or information disclosure via writes to higher exception level resources (CVE-2025-10263)\n\n* kernel: net: openvswitch: reject oversized nested action attrs (CVE-2026-64531)\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):\n\n* [RHEL 9.7] Core and x86 IOMMU subsystem update [rhel-9.4.z] (JIRA:RHEL-134805)\n\n* [xfstests xfs/017] xfs_repair fails and hit XFS: Assertion failed: 0, file: fs/xfs/xfs_icache.c, line: 1840 [rhel-9.4.z] (JIRA:RHEL-188770)\n\n* nfs: backport patch which checks delegation validity in nfs_start_delegation_return_locked to RHEL 9 [rhel-9.4.z] (JIRA:RHEL-212041)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
